Implementation in `lru_ttl.py`: an `OrderedDict` keyed by key, each entry holding `(value, expires_at)` where `expires_at = clock() + ttl` at put time (`None` when `ttl=None`). Recency is the dict order — `get` hits call `move_to_end`, `put` inserts fresh and moves to end; `__contains__` and `__len__` check liveness without touching order. An entry is expired once `clock() >= expires_at`; `get` deletes expired entries and returns `default`, and `put` purges all expired entries before evicting LRU (`popitem(last=False)`) until at most `capacity` remain. `capacity < 1` raises `ValueError`. Standard library only (`time`, `collections.OrderedDict`).", "r": "All 11 tests passed. Done. Brief report.
